TITLE: Plan membership and collection contradict
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: prose
STATEMENT: >>>
A node belongs to a plan by directory, while the one-grammar ruling says membership is an edge that 112 groomed nodes lack. Work 'dies with its plan', yet six pieces of work hold their proof in NOTES and twelve durable nodes point at probes whose work half would die. Collecting a plan today either breaks the export or deletes evidence.

Nodes it touches: [LINK: DEC-ONE-GRAMMAR], [LINK: DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN], [LINK: MECH-PLAN-CHANGE-KINDS], [LINK: MECH-PLAN-BEADS-SNAPSHOT], [LINK: MECH-SPIKE-IS-A-PIPELINE-TO-A-DECISION] and [LINK: SLICE-SDOC-IN-SEMBLE].
<<<
